                "evidence": "review changes_requested: duetflow/app.py:160-168 and 223-228 newly route `duetflow collect` through refresh_access_token, but an expired refresh token (`400 invalid_grant`) is neither marked unusable nor reported with the affected role. Given a stored account whose access token is stale and whose refresh response is invalid_grant, this Collection exits with only the generic instruction to re-run consent for \u2018this account\u2019; the unchanged account remains eligible, so every later hourly Collection sends the same expired refresh token again. docs/PLAN.md \u00a75 requires invalid_grant to be non-retried, the account to be marked, and the operator to be told `duetflow auth --user X`; failing that credential-lifecycle behavior makes the new public Collection path repeatedly hit a terminal auth failure without an actionable role-specific recovery command.",
